  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f424be585f9e04c79a96c8292e8b9db1, type: 3}
  m_Name: Conceito_SmartCity
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Metis.Runtime::KnowledgeEntryData
  _title: Smart City
  _titleEn: Smart City
  _category: 2
  _unlockTrigger: 9
  _summary: "Smart city \xE9 a cidade que usa dados e tecnologia para planejar e
    operar seus servi\xE7os de forma integrada. O termo \xE9 disputado: para alguns,
    \xE9 efici\xEAncia; para outros, deve servir antes de tudo \xE0s pessoas."
  _summaryEn: 'A smart city uses data and technology to plan and run its services
    in an integrated way. The term is contested: for some it means efficiency; for
    others it must serve people first.'
  _realWorld: "O Centro de Opera\xE7\xF5es Rio, inaugurado em 2010, integra dezenas
    de \xF3rg\xE3os da prefeitura numa sala s\xF3; j\xE1 Songdo, na Coreia do Sul,
    foi constru\xEDda do zero como cidade inteligente e demorou a atrair moradores."
  _realWorldEn: Rio de Janeiro's Operations Center, opened in 2010, brings dozens
    of city agencies into a single room; Songdo, in South Korea, was built from scratch
    as a smart city and was slow to attract residents.
  _tradeOffs: "Tecnologia sem participa\xE7\xE3o pode virar vigil\xE2ncia ou vitrine;
    o resultado depende de para quem ela \xE9 desenhada."
  _tradeOffsEn: Technology without participation can turn into surveillance or a
    showcase; the outcome depends on who it is designed for.
  _sources:
  - Label: Smart city (Wikipedia)
    Url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smart_city
  - Label: "Centro de Opera\xE7\xF5es Rio (Wikip\xE9dia)"
    Url: https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centro_de_Opera%C3%A7%C3%B5es_Rio
  - Label: Songdo (Wikipedia)
    Url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Songdo_International_Business_District
